[{"id":2568431939,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6ZFylD","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"06cba6054b201f8590879f289a5b16cb819af2ff","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected.\r\n\r\n**Testing project:** [test_pr_101471.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18512374/test_pr_101471.zip)\r\n\r\nAn example CSV where different languages have a different number of plural forms will look like this:\r\n\r\n```csv\r\nKEY,en,fr,lt,jp\r\n_PluralRule,plurals=2; plural=(n != 1);,nplurals=2; plural=n>1;,nplurals=3; plural=n%10==1 && n%100!=11 ? 0 : n%10>=2 && (n%100<10 || n%100>=20) ? 1 : 2;,nplurals=1; plural=0;\r\nAPPLE_COUNT,There is %d apple,Il y a %d pomme,yra %d obuolys,リンゴが%d個あります\r\nAPPLE_COUNT,There are %d apples,Il y a %d pommes,yra %d obuoliai,\r\nAPPLE_COUNT,,,yra %d obuolių,\r\nAPPLE_COUNT,,,,\r\nAPPLE_COUNT2,[2] There is %d apple,[2] Il y a %d pomme,[2] yra %d obuolys,[2] リンゴが%d個あります\r\nAPPLE_COUNT2,[2] There are %d apples,[2] Il y a %d pommes,[2] yra %d obuoliai,\r\nAPPLE_COUNT2,,,[2] yra %d obuolių,\r\nAPPLE_COUNT2,,,,\r\n```\r\n\r\nLanguages which don't have as many plural forms as the language with the most plural forms in the CSV should have empty fields.\r\n\r\nRegarding usability, it can be difficult to find the expected plural forms for each language yourself. I've landed on [the gettext manual](https://www.gnu.org/software/gettext/manual/html_node/Plural-forms.html) where I found the plural forms I needed and had to carefully copy-paste them into the CSV (while making sure they are on a single line). Could we have our own database of plural forms and automatically infer them instead if no `_PluralRule` line is found in the CSV? This would eliminate the need for users to specify a `_PluralRule` line in most cases.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101471#pullrequestreview-2568431939","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101471","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-01-22T22:31:50Z"},{"id":2699717189,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6g6mpF","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"06cba6054b201f8590879f289a5b16cb819af2ff","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?u=8069d9b7bc6ab503ce83dfcfa53fd021672aeccf&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","login":"Mickeon","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101471#pullrequestreview-2699717189","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101471","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-03-19T19:01:15Z"},{"id":2700188816,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6g8ZyQ","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"06cba6054b201f8590879f289a5b16cb819af2ff","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?u=2867ee7fcd920bc19b7d1cbf4b10264b9bbc9326&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","login":"bruvzg","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg"}